  "unresolved": [
    "The independent lattice benzene has large anisotropic displacement parameters consistent with unresolved motion/disorder. A two-orientation PART/SADI trial worsened R1 and wR2; the one-site model was retained with six DFIX 1.390(10) A and FLAT 0.01 A restraints.",
    "Residual density is about +1.8/-1.6 e A^-3. The strongest positive peaks near N3/alkyl and La/Ni environments have no unambiguous chemically valid atom assignment; no chemistry-free atoms were added.",
    "The supplied HKLF4 contains only independent reflections, so an experimental R_int cannot be reconstructed. Overall completeness is 0.741 to d_min 0.682 A; theta-full completeness is 0.907.",
    "Crystal temperature, dimensions, colour/habit, cell-measurement reflection range/count and absorption-correction details are incomplete in context.json and must be supplied for a complete journal CIF.",
    "A reindexed TWINABS HKLF5 refinement gave BASF 0.00875 with no meaningful improvement over HKLF4; the twin component was not retained."
  ],
  "summary_note": "SHELXT 2018/2 solved P-1 (R1 0.130, Rweak 0.016, CFOM 0.8715; C44 N8 P2 Ni La). TWINABS HKLF5 was reindexed by h5=-h4, k5=-k4, l5=h4+k4+l4 and refined to BASF 0.00875 without meaningful improvement, so HKLF4 was retained. A rigid two-orientation lattice-benzene PART trial refined to 0.627/0.373 but worsened R1/wR2 and was rejected. The one-site lattice benzene required six DFIX C-C=1.390(10) A and FLAT 0.01 A restraints because unresolved motion otherwise gave PLAT331-A geometry; no restraints affect the La/Ni complex and no solvent mask was used. SHELXL weighting converged at approximately 0.0925/8.31 and final maximum shift/s.u. is 0.001.",
